    "OverallSummary": "In this case, George Snyder IV willfully violated the Care Obligation under Regulation Best Interest by recommending leveraged exchange-traded funds (NT-ETPs) and crypto mining stocks to 18 retail customers without: (1) understanding the features and risks of these products, including the holding-period risk of NT-ETPs and volatility of the stocks; (2) conducting any research about the products or reviewing their prospectuses; and (3) analyzing whether the investments were in the best interest of each customer based on their individual investment profiles. Between January and August 2022, Snyder recommended 33 purchases to 18 customers who had minimal or no prior experience with these investments. Six customers were senior investors, and seven customers (including two senior investors) had conservative or moderate risk tolerances. The customers suffered total realized losses of approximately $30,000, while Snyder received $3,699.03 in commissions. Additionally, Snyder mismarked 32 order tickets as unsolicited when they were solicited and exercised discretion in customer accounts without written authorization. FINRA imposed sanctions including a five-month suspension, $10,000 fine, and disgorgement of commissions plus interest. Ameriprise offered rescission of the relevant transactions to affected customers."
